 "notes": [
  "Continuation is measured on summaries that have all nine headings and fit the budget; the others score zero whatever it would be.",
  "33 of the 306 planted facts sit only in the agent's thinking blocks, which the canonical rendering does not carry, so 273 is the most a contestant can recall.",
  "Cost for the miner models is 4090 time at the pod's hourly price plus the list price of 0.01 USD per million input tokens with output free; the base model is 4090 time only.",
  "Qwen 3.8 27B and Gemma 4 31B are the open weight models the study itself ran, in the same quantised files. They ran on rented 48 GB cards with llama.cpp, thinking off, one request at a time, and their cost is card time at the pod's hourly price. Closed API models are not in this run.",
  "Qwen 3.8 27B is the reader and Gemma 4 31B the judge, with one vote per reply because the judge is deterministic. Qwen rescored a quarter of the replies and the two agreed with a kappa of 0.51, so the commitment column is noisy.",
  "The Pi prompt contestant writes Pi's own summary format, so it cannot pass the arena's format gate. Read its planted fact and commitment columns.",
  "For 21 of the 72 Qwen summaries the stream dropped and resumed from the server's cache, so their time is the measured generation time plus prompt time fitted on the other rows."
 ],
